<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anti-Revolutionary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as ARP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anti-Revolutionary Party was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Protestant political party founded in 1879 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-kuyper">Abraham Kuyper</a>, the first national mass party in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. Rejecting the principles of the French Revolution, it fought for state funding of religious schools, won in 1917, and took part in many coalition governments. In 1980 it merged with Catholic and other Protestant parties to form the Christian Democratic Appeal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anti-revolutionary-party.jpg" alt="Anti-Revolutionary Party" width="320" height="124" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: ARP Vector: Strepulah · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anti-Revolutionaire_Partij_logo_(1968-1980).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
